---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "@utils/site";
const updated = "2026-05-06";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The rules of using Pocketey: ownership of the games, what you may and may not do with the site, and how disputes are handled."
  pageType="static"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-amber-400 text-stroke-ink">
      Terms of Use
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-60">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed">
      Welcome to {SITE.name}. By using this site or playing any of the games
      hosted on it, you agree to the terms set out below. If you do not agree
      with any part of them, please do not use the site. We try to keep these
      terms readable; legal jargon is kept to the minimum required to be
      enforceable.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Free to play, paid by ads</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      All games on {SITE.name} are provided free of charge. The site is funded
      by advertising. We reserve the right to add, change, or remove ad
      placements at any time. We do not currently sell in-game items, season
      passes, or accounts; if that ever changes, the change will be reflected
      in the relevant game and these terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Intellectual property</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      All games, source code, art, audio, copy, branding, and design on the
      site are the property of the {SITE.name} project and its contributors,
      except where third-party assets are explicitly credited. You may share
      links to public pages of the site, embed game pages on your own site
      using the standard URL inside an iframe, take screenshots and video
      recordings for personal use, reviews, or news coverage, and stream
      gameplay on platforms such as YouTube and Twitch.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      You may not copy or redistribute the game code or assets, repackage
      them as a separate product, sell access to them, or remove or obscure
      attribution and ad placements within the games themselves. If you would
      like to use anything beyond the scope of personal sharing, please use
      the contact page first.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      You agree not to use the site in ways that are illegal, that interfere
      with other users, or that compromise the integrity of the games. That
      includes attempting to break or bypass anti-cheat measures, scraping
      the site at a rate that strains the host, attempting to inject code
      into a game frame, or impersonating other users in any community
      discussion that may exist around a game. The site is intentionally
      account-free; please respect that openness.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">No warranty</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      The site and all games are provided on an "as-is" basis, without
      warranty of any kind. We try hard to keep things working and to test on
      the major mobile browsers, but we cannot guarantee that every game will
      run correctly on every device, that the site will be available without
      interruption, or that high scores stored on your device will survive
      browser updates or cache clears. Save anything important elsewhere.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, {SITE.name} and its
      operator shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential or punitive damages arising out of your use of the site
      or any of the games. Total liability for any claim related to the site
      will not exceed the amount you paid to use it, which for free play is
      zero.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Third-party services</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      Some pages display content from third parties such as ad networks,
      embeds from social platforms, or links to other web sites. Their
      behavior is governed by their own terms and privacy policies. We are
      not responsible for the availability, accuracy, or conduct of those
      services.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      We may update these terms from time to time. The updated date at the
      top of the page reflects the most recent revision. Continued use of the
      site after a change indicates acceptance of the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      For questions about these terms, please use the
      <a class="underline" href="/contact/">contact page</a>. For privacy
      matters, see the
      <a class="underline" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
